{
  "id": "p23",
  "title": "Election Night in the Old District",
  "titleZh": "老选区的选举之夜",
  "topic": "地区选举",
  "paragraphs": [
    [
      {
        "en": "The central system of this quiet campaign is simple and clear.",
        "zh": "这场平静竞选的中央系统简单又清晰。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Our regional paper sends me to shoot photos in a busy district.",
        "zh": "我们地区报纸派我去一个繁忙的选区拍摄照片。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The premier will speak tonight, and every headline waits.",
        "zh": "总理今晚将讲话，每条头条都在等待。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The ballot count will rank each party by its full name.",
        "zh": "点票结果将按全名排列每个政党的名次。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A minimum percentage decides who may enter the crowded hall.",
        "zh": "一个最低百分比决定谁能进入拥挤的大厅。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Votes reach a peak shortly after the tall doors close.",
        "zh": "高大的门关上后不久，票数达到峰值。"
      },
      {
        "en": "My first award as a young reporter still inspires me.",
        "zh": "我作为年轻记者获得的第一个奖项至今激励着我。"
      },
      {
        "en": "I must persuade myself to stay calm and fully conscious.",
        "zh": "我必须说服自己保持冷静和完全清醒。"
      },
      {
        "en": "My priority recently is to pursue the plain truth, not gossip.",
        "zh": "我最近的优先事项是追求朴素的事实，而不是闲话。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Ultimately, a sophisticated reader wants clear facts, not noise.",
        "zh": "最终，成熟的读者想要清晰的事实，而不是噪音。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "A dark suspicion and an ugly rumour spread through the crowd.",
        "zh": "一个阴暗的猜疑和一条丑陋的谣言在人群中传开。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A loud clash makes a tired guard rage outside the gate.",
        "zh": "一场激烈的冲突让疲惫的卫兵在门外暴怒。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Then I reckon the long delay will frustrate every waiting crowd.",
        "zh": "然后我估计漫长的延迟会让每个等待的人群沮丧。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The chairman rejects my sharp question with a cold smile.",
        "zh": "主席带着冷笑拒绝了我尖锐的问题。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Later I spot one small error in the printed list of names.",
        "zh": "后来我在打印的名单上发现一个小错误。"
      },
      {
        "en": "I consult my old notes and choose a careful phrase.",
        "zh": "我查阅旧笔记，选了一个谨慎的说法。"
      },
      {
        "en": "My editor sighs at the mess on my crowded desk.",
        "zh": "我的编辑对着我拥挤办公桌上的乱摊子叹气。"
      },
      {
        "en": "His insurance covers the property beside the old food market.",
        "zh": "他的保险覆盖了老食品市场旁边的房产。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A broker sells a small apartment near the busy station.",
        "zh": "一位经纪人出售车站附近的一间小公寓。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Their white cottage has a wooden deck and a green roof.",
        "zh": "他们的白色小屋有一个木制露台和绿色屋顶。"
      }
    ],
    [
      {
        "en": "The city charter protects a treaty signed many years ago.",
        "zh": "城市宪章保护着一份多年前签署的条约。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Then a new threat may extend the peace talks into next week.",
        "zh": "然后一个新的威胁可能把和谈延长到下周。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A radical plan would define the old town in new words.",
        "zh": "一个激进的计划会用新词重新定义这座老镇。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The idea began elsewhere, but its true origin is local.",
        "zh": "这个想法始于别处，但真正的源头在本地。"
      },
      {
        "en": "Soft jazz plays while new software counts every single vote.",
        "zh": "柔和的爵士乐响起，新软件统计着每一张选票。"
      },
      {
        "en": "The final numbers are fairly clear and precisely checked.",
        "zh": "最终的数字相当清楚，也经过精确核对。"
      },
      {
        "en": "My pregnant sister treats every guest with gentle care.",
        "zh": "我怀孕的姐姐温柔地招待每一位客人。"
      },
      {
        "en": "A civil word can build a strong bond between old rivals.",
        "zh": "一句客气的话能在老对手之间建立牢固的纽带。"
      }
    ]
  ],
